  "title": "Friendly partitions",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "A friendly partition of a graph is a partition of the vertices into two sets so that every vertex has at least as many neighbours in its own class as in the other.\n\nProblem Is it true that for every $r$, all but finitely many $r$-regular graphs have friendly partitions?",
